# Line endings
#
# The repository stores every text file with LF. Working copies get whatever
# the platform uses, so Windows checkouts are CRLF and nothing has to be
# configured per machine. This replaces relying on core.autocrlf, which is a
# per-clone setting and was different on different checkouts of this repo.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree. Git for Windows runs them
# through sh, and a CR at the end of a line becomes part of the command.
# Governance/.githooks/pre-push is the one that matters here.
*.sh text eol=lf
Governance/.githooks/** text eol=lf

# Images. Every one of these is in the tree or will be: icons, sidebar
# artwork, splash screens, and the photos used as test fixtures.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.bmp binary
*.webp binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.heic binary
*.heif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary

# Fonts.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ttc binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Other binaries that turn up around a construction app.
*.pdf binary
*.dwg binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
